hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15794","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Abu Shu'bah narrating from Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, that a man slapped a servant girl of the family of Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, and Suwayd said to him: Do you not know that the face is forbidden? You saw me seventh of seven with my brothers, and we had only one servant. One of us slapped him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to free him."
"15795","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, he said: I heard a man from Banu Mazin narrating from Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with nabidh in a jar, and asked him about it, and he forbade me from it, so I took the jar and broke it."
"15796","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Suwayd, he said: I slapped a freedman of ours, then I came, my father at Zuhr, and prayed with him. When he greeted, he took my hand and said: Take retribution from him, and he pardoned. Then he began narrating. He said: We, the sons of Muqarrin, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were seven, and we had only one maidservant. One of us slapped her, and it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Free her. They said: We have no servant but her. He said: Let them employ her, and when they can do without her, let them free her way."
